# AUTO-CAD 2D LAB MANUAL (FINAL – ACADEMIC VERSION)
# Experiment 1: Detail & Assembly Drawing using AutoCAD (2D)
* 1. Objective

To create 2D detailed and assembly drawings of basic machine components using AutoCAD with proper dimensioning and A3 sheet layout.

* 2. Software & Tools
AutoCAD (2D)
Computer system
Standard drawing sheet (A3)
* 3. Drawing Standards (Simplified Academic)
Units: mm
Scale: 1:1
Projection: First Angle
Line types:
Object: Continuous thick
Center: Dashed
Dimension: Thin
* 4. A3 Sheet Layout
Sheet Size
420 × 297 mm
Margins
Left: 20 mm
Other sides: 10 mm
Title Block (Bottom Right)

Include:

Name
Roll No
Experiment No
Scale
Date
* 5. General AutoCAD Procedure
Open AutoCAD → New Drawing
Set Units (UNITS) → mm
Set Limits → 0,0 to 420,297
Create Layers (Object, Center, Dimension)
Draw using LINE, CIRCLE, ARC
Modify using OFFSET, TRIM, FILLET
Add Dimensions (DIM)
Add Hatch (for section)
Plot → A3 → Scale 1:1
* 6. COMPONENT DRAWINGS (WITH SIMPLE DIMENSIONS)
6.1 Plummer Block
Dimensions (mm)
Base: 120 × 80
Height: 80
Bearing hole: Ø40
Bolt holes: Ø10 (2 holes)
Bolt spacing: 80 mm
Steps
Draw base rectangle (120 × 80)
Draw centerline
Draw semicircle (Ø40) on top
Add side walls
Draw bolt holes
Apply hatch in section view
Add dimensions
6.2 Wall Bracket
Dimensions
Base: 100 × 60
Vertical height: 120
Rib thickness: 10
Holes: Ø10
Steps
Draw vertical plate
Draw horizontal base
Add inclined rib
Create holes
Dimension
6.3 Stepped Pulley
Dimensions
Outer diameters: Ø100, Ø80, Ø60
Shaft hole: Ø20
Width: 60
Steps
Draw centerline
Draw concentric circles
Offset for steps
Add keyway
Dimension diameters
6.4 Flanged Coupling
Dimensions
Flange diameter: Ø120
Shaft hole: Ø30
Bolt circle: Ø90
Bolt holes: Ø10 (4 holes)
Steps
Draw flange circle
Draw shaft hole
Create bolt circle
Use ARRAY for 4 bolts
Add section view
Dimension
6.5 Machine Tool Holder (3 Views)
Dimensions
Length: 100
Width: 40
Height: 60
Steps
Draw front view
Project top view
Project side view
Maintain alignment
Add dimensions
6.6 Screw Jack
Dimensions
Base: 80 × 80
Height: 150
Screw diameter: Ø25
Head: Ø50
Steps
Draw base
Draw vertical screw
Add head
Show section
Add dimensions
